  "worked_solution": "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }({sin}^{3}\u2061\\theta +{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta ) & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }\\cdot {sin}^{3}\u2061\\theta +\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }\\cdot {cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{3}\u2061\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }+\\frac{{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\cdot \\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }}+\\frac{{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }} \\\\  & ={sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta +{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta  \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, in the last step, we simplified the right-hand side using ${cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta +{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta =1.$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }({sin}^{3}\u2061\\theta +{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta )=1.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
